---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = "Logo Trademark Registration in India | Device Mark Protection";
const description = "Protect your visual identity, emblems, icons, and graphic logos with a device mark registration in India. Guidance on artwork and filing with BRNDNUR.";
const canonical = "https://brndnur.com/logo-trademark-registration/";
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonical={canonical}
  currentPath="/logo-trademark-registration/"
>
  <main id="main-content">
    <!-- Breadcrumb & Hero -->
    <section class="page-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <nav class="bn-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
          <a href="/">Home</a>
          <span class="sep">/</span>
          <a href="/services/">Services</a>
          <span class="sep">/</span>
          <span class="current">Logo Trademark Registration</span>
        </nav>
        <p class="eyebrow">Visual Identity Protection</p>
        <h1>Logo & Device Mark Trademark Registration.</h1>
        <p class="lead">Your logo represents your company’s public face. Registering a device mark protects the specific graphic composition, artistic emblem, custom typography, and visual brand identity submitted to the Trade Marks Registry.</p>
        
        <div class="hero-badges">
          <div class="hero-badge-item">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="4"/><line x1="21.17" y1="8" x2="12" y2="8"/><line x1="3.95" y1="6.06" x2="8.54" y2="14"/><line x1="10.88" y1="21.94" x2="15.46" y2="14"/></svg>
            <span>Device Mark & Emblem Protection</span>
          </div>
          <div class="hero-badge-item">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="18" rx="2" ry="2"/><circle cx="8.5" cy="8.5" r="1.5"/><polyline points="21 15 16 10 5 21"/></svg>
            <span>Vienna Codification Compliant</span>
          </div>
          <div class="hero-badge-item">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/></svg>
            <span>Packaging & Counterfeit Defense</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="actions" style="margin-top: 28px;">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://wa.me/919048188899?text=Hello%20BRNDNUR%2C%20I%20want%20to%20protect%20my%20logo." target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Protect Your Logo &rarr;</a>
          <a class="btn btn-outline" href="/wordmark-registration/">Explore Wordmarks</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Split Visual Section -->
    <section class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="split-row">
          <div class="split-photo">
            <img src="/services/assets/trademark-services.webp" alt="BRNDNUR Logo trademark registration artwork preparation in Kerala" width="800" height="600" loading="lazy" />
          </div>
          <div class="split-copy">
            <p class="eyebrow">Visual Defense</p>
            <h2>Protecting Your Graphic Elements & Packaging</h2>
            <p>Customers recognize products on supermarket shelves, delivery boxes, and digital mobile apps primarily by visual design—the distinctive emblem, geometric shapes, stylized mascot, and color palette.</p>
            <p>Under the Trade Marks Act, 1999, filing a Device Mark locks in your exclusive rights over the specific graphic presentation. When a competitor attempts to use a visually imitating emblem or deceptive packaging layout, a registered device mark provides definitive legal grounds to halt imitation.</p>
            <div class="advisory-notice" style="margin-top: 16px;">
              <div class="advisory-notice-icon">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><line x1="12" y1="8" x2="12" y2="12"/><line x1="12" y1="16" x2="12.01" y2="16"/></svg>
              </div>
              <div class="advisory-notice-content">
                <h4>Vienna Agreement Codification</h4>
                <p>Every device mark submitted in India is classified under the international Vienna Classification for figurative elements. Registry examiners assign specific numerical codes to geometric shapes, human figures, animals, and flora to detect graphical conflicts.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Filing Considerations with Clean SVGs -->
    <section class="section section-alt">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-heading text-center">
          <p class="eyebrow">Filing Requirements</p>
          <h2>Preparing Your Logo Artwork for Submission</h2>
          <p>Proper artwork preparation ensures smooth processing and eliminates technical objections from the registry examiner:</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card-grid">
          <div class="bn-card">
            <div class="card-icon" style="color: #A8781A;">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><path d="M12 2a14.5 14.5 0 0 0 0 20 10 10 0 0 0 0-20"/></svg>
            </div>
            <h3>Color vs. Black & White</h3>
            <p>Filing in black and white or grayscale generally grants protection across all color applications, whereas claiming specific colors limits rights to those exact shades.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="bn-card">
            <div class="card-icon" style="color: #A8781A;">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="18" rx="2" ry="2"/><line x1="3" y1="9" x2="21" y2="9"/><line x1="9" y1="21" x2="9" y2="9"/></svg>
            </div>
            <h3>Artwork Resolution & Sizing</h3>
            <p>The Trade Marks Registry mandates high-contrast digital representations within an 8cm x 8cm boundary, free of background watermarks or photographic artifacts.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="bn-card">
            <div class="card-icon" style="color: #A8781A;">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/><circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/></svg>
            </div>
            <h3>Composite Mark Rights</h3>
            <p>If your logo contains both a unique emblem and text, a device mark protects the combined whole. Filing both a wordmark and a logo offers maximum brand defense.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Artwork Specification & Vienna Guidelines Table -->
    <section class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-heading text-center">
          <p class="eyebrow">Registry Guidelines</p>
          <h2>Artwork & Specimen Standards (Form TM-A)</h2>
          <p>Technical requirements mandated by the Indian Trade Marks Registry for device applications.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="bn-table-wrap">
          <table class="bn-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Requirement</th>
                <th>Standard Specification</th>
                <th>Advisory Recommendation</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>Image Format & Size</strong></td>
                <td>JPEG/PNG, 8cm x 8cm bounding box, &lt; 5MB</td>
                <td>Supply vector or high-resolution (300 DPI) source files</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>Color Limitation Claim</strong></td>
                <td>Specific color combinations can be claimed</td>
                <td>File in black & white unless color combination is your primary differentiator</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>Non-English / Vernacular Text</strong></td>
                <td>Mandatory transliteration and translation into English</td>
                <td>Submit transliteration affidavit if mark includes Malayalam, Arabic, or Hindi script</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>Composite Mark Strategy</strong></td>
                <td>Protects logo emblem + wordmark arrangement as a unit</td>
                <td>Pair with a standalone wordmark to prevent competitors from using the name separately</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Call to Action -->
    <section class="cta-section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="cta-panel">
          <p class="eyebrow">Secure Your Emblem</p>
          <h2>Ensure No Competitor Copies Your Visual Identity.</h2>
          <p>Send us your logo files. We will review the artwork against classification guidelines and prepare your application.</p>
          <div class="cta-actions">
            <a class="btn btn-gold" href="https://wa.me/919048188899?text=Hello%20BRNDNUR%2C%20here%20is%20my%20logo%20for%20review." target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Submit Logo for Review &rarr;</a>
            <a class="btn btn-outline" href="/trademark-registration/">View Overall Process</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
